    "explanation": "Ruling for both parties — and for the rider, the short answer is that the money cannot move on this record.\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS. The fare is METERED (EV-FARE-00806), charged_total SGD 13.03, with surge_multiplier 1.0 read from the fare breakdown (the trip record does not carry the field). The platform's optimal route at booking (EV-TRIP-00806) was 4.0 km / 12.0 min. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00806) measures 5.56 km, an excess of 1.56 km / 39.00% — enough to clear POL-RD-01's establishment gates (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) but below its material thresholds (50% / 8.0 km). So no MATERIAL deviation and no POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral arises in any event.\n\nTHE TRACE CANNOT CARRY THE FINDING. EV-GPS-00806 is impaired: weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW — a 160-second gap between 14:03:50 and 14:06:30, fifteen consecutive 10-second fixes absent, the polyline joining the bounding fixes directly. That is the schema pre-pass tag, and it is separately a policy-level impairment under POL-RD-07(a), because the gap exceeds 90 seconds inside the disputed segment; the ruling says both things. Under POL-RD-07(ii) a deviation may NOT be established on an impaired trace alone and needs one of four independent sources, and none exists: EV-CHAT-00806 holds 0 messages (no driver admission); EV-FARE-00806 charges no erp_gantries that would place the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use; the counterparty statement is null; and trip_record.actual_distance_km and fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km are, by their own admissibility notes, copies of this same trace rather than independent measurements. POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) therefore require ESCALATE, and POL-RD-10(1) is independently engaged: confidence is capped at 0.6 under POL-GEN-02(2) because the impaired trace is the artifact carrying the deciding fact, and 0.6 is below the 0.70 floor. Both money fields are null and the SGD 13.03 is HELD, not collected and not refunded.\n\nTO THE RIDER. Your distance point is well made on the numbers (5.56 km trace against 4.0 km optimal) and the POL-RD-02 arithmetic you offered is correct — recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 4.0 + 0.28 x 12.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 + 0.00 ERP + 0.00 waiting - 0.00 promo = 10.96; refund = 13.03 - 10.96 = 2.07, above the 0.50 de minimis, rounded up to 2.10. It cannot issue, because the only artifact that measures the distance is impaired and nothing independent supports it; the escalation replaces that figure rather than granting it. Your profile claim is also accepted: deviation_claims_60d is 0 and no further corroboration is demanded of you.\n\nTO THE DRIVER. Your points are accepted and they are what drives the escalation: there is no independent corroboration of the excess; there is no repeat-deviation pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 300, far below the POL-RD-06 gate), so no balance is resolved against you and no conduct referral arises; and there is no billing-integrity defect — no ERP gantries, no toll lines, no airport surcharge — so nothing is refundable under POL-RD-09(4). The profile mentions the referee flagged (rating, acceptance_rate, prior_disputes_filed, prior_deviation_flags) were cited by both sides only to say they are context-only under POL-GEN-01, and no finding rests on them.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT. An independent distance record (an odometer or metered export not derived from this trace), a driver admission in the chat log, ERP gantry records placing the vehicle off the optimal corridor, or a counterparty statement — any one of these would let the deviation be established and the POL-RD-02 arithmetic run. The reviewer has the full case summary, both briefs and the admissibility report, and the appeal route under POL-GEN-04 is available."
